From b3f0336593beafc244ba9d7a00c2c430287ab70a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kopebax <kopebax@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:25:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gps: keep the legacy XTRA interface without system_server

The native XTRA client 2.0 in libizat_core only runs inside Android's
system_server. On Sailfish OS its mere presence made loc_eng_xtra_init()
refuse the XTRA interface, so no assistance data was ever downloaded and
cold starts took minutes. Always offer the interface; the location service
downloads and injects the data itself.

Developed with the assistance of Claude (Anthropic).
---
 gps/loc_api/libloc_api_50001/loc_eng_xtra.cpp | 10 ++++------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gps/loc_api/libloc_api_50001/loc_eng_xtra.cpp b/gps/loc_api/libloc_api_50001/loc_eng_xtra.cpp
index d334e0a..aa8f504 100644
--- a/gps/loc_api/libloc_api_50001/loc_eng_xtra.cpp
+++ b/gps/loc_api/libloc_api_50001/loc_eng_xtra.cpp
@@ -124,12 +124,10 @@ int loc_eng_xtra_init (loc_eng_data_s_type &loc_eng_data,
     loc_eng_xtra_data_s_type *xtra_module_data_ptr;
     ENTRY_LOG();
 
-    if(!loc_eng_data.adapter->mSupportsTimeInjection
-       || loc_eng_data.adapter->hasNativeXtraClient()) {
-        LOC_LOGD("XTRA is already supported. disable it here.\n");
-        EXIT_LOG(%d, 1); // return 1 denote failure
-        return 1;
-    }
+    // The native XTRA client 2.0 (libizat_core) and the LBS services that
+    // would otherwise handle XTRA only run inside Android's system_server.
+    // Without them (e.g. on Sailfish OS) always offer the legacy XTRA
+    // interface so the location service can download and inject XTRA data.
 
     if(callbacks == NULL) {
         LOC_LOGE("loc_eng_xtra_init: failed, cb is NULL");
-- 
2.56.0

